ct storm  there were so many factors involved  early on  the data that the government presented  to  the people was that mass don't work and  it came out that it  wasn't that mass didn't work they didn't  want people to purchase masks because  there weren't enough masks for the  healthcare workers  also only the cdc could make the kova  test kit and they picked their primers  and probes  to target even though other countries  had already created test kits so there  really is no standardized test kit  everyone's using different test kits  that they've created within their  country  multiplex versus a single test the cdc  made a much more complex  coronavirus test initially and that  later they moved to a single target  single test configuration  other negative controls were  contaminated we've also found out that  some of the laboratories ran the cycles  too long so that everything would come  up positive  so with all the false positives out  there it was really difficult to  understand  the true picture of the the outbreak in  the country  there was a shortage of ppe a lot of it  was coming from  china there were quality issues  hospitals were overwhelmed  in many cases in italy where people were  on life support they were making  decisions based on the age of the  patient so it was a really horrible time  later masks do work where to if it makes  you feel safe so  there was so much misinformation  confusing information being  provided then finally we write about  contaminated vaccines where  millions of doses were disposed of and  all the while there were cases cases  cases clusters  of the outbreak continuing and then just  boom  full-blown pandemic  our final case study is looking at  manufacturing issues  vaccine development challenges by  pharmaceutical companies  all related to product quality there's a  manufacturing  facility called emergent they were  located in baltimore they were actually  making the vaccines for both  johnson and johnson as well as  astr